# skill: memory-static

## Contract
Static memory allocation patterns for C. No dynamic allocation (malloc/calloc/realloc/free). Memory is allocated at compile time or within static storage.

## Dependencies
None

## Slots
- `STATIC_BUFFER(name, size)` — Declare a static buffer with given name and size
- `StaticBuffer` struct — Buffer with data pointer, capacity, and length tracker
- `static_buffer_init()` — Initialize a StaticBuffer with static storage

## Boundaries
- Buffer size must be known at compile time
- Static storage has fixed size (256 int default in init)
- No runtime resizing or allocation

## Examples

```c
// Declare a static buffer with max size
#define STATIC_BUFFER(name, size) \
    static int name[size]

// Static buffer with current length tracker
struct StaticBuffer {
    int* data;
    int capacity;
    int length;
};

// Initialize a static buffer
void static_buffer_init(struct StaticBuffer* buf, int capacity) {
    static int storage[256];
    buf->data = storage;
    buf->capacity = capacity;
    buf->length = 0;
}
```
